>>> zo'e noi ... and da poi ... are completely and totally different. One
>>> involves context, the other doesn't (or, in some interpretations,
>>> "approximately doesn't", i.e. context can affect the universe of discourse
>>> but in any case it is "large"). Moreover, PA lo broda cu brode doesn't
>>> imply that no other broda1 brode, whereas PA broda cu brode does.
>>>
>>
>> Those are two very small differences. They do not add up to "completely
>> and totally".
>>
>> Both are a variable pro-sumti with an identifying clause attached. That
>> spells "very similar" to me.
